<article class="env-definition" id="0ENL">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0ENL">Definition <span data-tag="0ENL">72.6.4</span>.</a> Let $S$ be a scheme. Let $X$ be a locally Noetherian integral algebraic space over $S$. Let $f \in R(X)^*$. For every prime divisor $Z \subset X$ we define the <em>order of vanishing of $f$ along $Z$</em> as the integer </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \text{ord}_ Z(f) = \text{length}_{\mathcal{O}_{X, \xi }^ h} (\mathcal{O}_{X, \xi }^ h/a \mathcal{O}_{X, \xi }^ h) - \text{length}_{\mathcal{O}_{X, \xi }^ h} (\mathcal{O}_{X, \xi }^ h/b \mathcal{O}_{X, \xi }^ h)  \]
</div>
  <p> where $a, b \in \mathcal{O}_{X, \xi }^ h$ are nonzerodivisors such that the image of $f$ in $Q(\mathcal{O}_{X, \xi }^ h)$ (Lemma <a href="/tag/0ENK" data-tag="0ENK">72.6.3</a>) is equal to $a/b$. This is well defined by Algebra, Lemma <a href="/tag/02MC" data-tag="02MC">10.121.1</a>. </p>
</article>